hadiths[31]{hadithnumber,text}:
"815","Jabir said, \A man had a child and named him al-Qasim. We said"
"816","Here is the translated text in English:Sa'id b. Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: Abu Gassan narrated to us, saying: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Sahl, saying: Al-Munzir b. Abi Usayd was brought to the Prophet (peace be upon him) when he was born, and he was placed on his thigh. Abu Usayd was sitting, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) pointed to something in front of him, and he ordered Abu Usayd to take his son and place him on the Prophet's (peace be upon him) thigh. The Prophet (peace be upon him) then asked, ""Where is the young one?"" Abu Usayd replied, ""We have wrapped him, O Messenger of Allah."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked, ""What is his name?"" Abu Usayd replied, ""Fulan."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""No, but his name is Al-Munzir."" So he was named Al-Munzir on that day."
"817","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \The name which hates the most is that a\nman be called the King of Kings.\"""""
"818","Talq ibn Habib said, \I was the most vehement person in denying\nintercession. I questioned Jabir and he said"
"819","Hanzala ibn Hidhaym said, \The Prophet"
"820","Ibn 'Umar said that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, changed a woman's name from 'Asiya (rebellious), saying, \You\nare Jamila (beautiful).\"""""
"821","Here is the translated text in English:Ali bin Abdullah and Sa'id bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Yaqub bin Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad bin Ishaq, saying: Muhammad bin 'Amr bin 'Ata' narrated to me, that he entered upon Zaynab bint Abi Salmah, and she asked him about the name of her sister who was with him. He said: I said, ""Her name is Barrah."" She said, ""Change her name."" For the Prophet (peace be upon him) married Zaynab bint Jahsh and her name was Barrah, so he changed her name to Zaynab. He entered upon Umm Salmah when he married her, and my name is Barrah. She heard me calling out, ""Barrah,"" and said, ""Do not purify yourselves, for Allah is more knowledgeable about the Barrah and the Fajirah among you."" She said, ""She is Zaynab."" I said to her, ""Name her."" She said, ""Change it to what the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) changed it to."" She said, ""Name her Zaynab."""
"822","Ibn 'Abdu'r-Rahman ibn Sa'id al-Makhzumi, whose name was as-Surm,\nreported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him\npeace, named him Sa'id (happy). He related that he had seen 'Uthman reclining\nin the mosque."
"823","Here is the translated text in English:Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani' bin Hani', from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When Hasan was born, I named him Harb. Then the Prophet came and said: Show me my son, what did you name him? We said: Harb. He said: No, he is Hasan. Then when Husayn was born, I named him Harb. Then the Prophet came and said: Show me my son, what did you name him? We said: Harb. He said: No, he is Husayn. Then when the third one was born, I named him Harb. Then the Prophet came and said: Show me my son, what did you name him? We said: Harb. He said: No, he is Muhassin. Then he said: I named them with the names of the children of Harun: Shibru, Shabir, and Mushabbir."
"824","It is reported that al-Harith ibn Abza said, \I was present at\nHunayn with the Prophet"
"825","'A'isha said, \A man called Shihab (flame) was mentioned in the\npresence of the Messenger of Allah"
"826","He narrated to us, Musaddad, saying: He narrated to us, Yahya bin Sa'id, from Zakariya, saying: He narrated to me, 'Amir, from 'Abdullah bin Muti', saying: I heard Muti' saying: I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, saying: On the day of the conquest of Mecca: No Qureshi will be killed patiently after this day until the Day of Resurrection. None of the people of 'Usah Qureshi will attain Islam except Muti', whose name was 'As, and the Prophet, peace be upon him, named him Muti'."
"827","'A'isha said that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \'A'ish! Jibril sends you greetings.\"" She said"
"828","Umm Kulthum, the daughter of Thumama, related that she went out\nto answer a call of nature,. Her brother, al-Makhariq ibn Thumama, said,\n\Go to 'A'isha and ask her about 'Uthman ibn 'Affan. People have said a\nlot about him. She said"
"829","Here is the translated text in English:Sulayman bin Harb narrated to us, saying: Al-Aswad bin Shayban narrated to us, saying: Khalid bin Sumayr narrated to us, saying: Bashir bin Nahik narrated to me, saying: Bashir narrated to us, saying: I came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and said: What is your name? He said: Zahn, he said: No, you are Bashir. While I was accompanying the Prophet, peace be upon him, he said: O son of the blacksmith, what have you woken up to do with Allah? Have you woken up to follow the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him? I said: By my father and mother, I have not woken up to do anything with Allah, I have only obtained good. Then he went to the graves of the polytheists and said: Indeed, these people have been preceded by a great deal of good. Then he went to the graves of the Muslims and said: Indeed, these people have been seized by a great deal of good. If a man has two sandals on his feet as he walks between the graves, he said: O companion of the two sandals, throw away your sandals, and he removed his own sandals."
"830","Part of previous hadith.\n\nحَدَّثَنَا سَعِيدُ بْنُ مَنْصُورٍ، قَالَ: حَدَّثَنَا عُبَيْدُ اللهِ بْنُ إِيَادٍ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ لَيْلَى امْرَأَةَ بَشِيرٍ تُحَدِّثُ، عَنْ بَشِيرِ ابْنِ الْخَصَاصِيَةِ، وَكَانَ اسْمُهُ زَحْمًا، فَسَمَّاهُ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم بَشِيرًا."
"831","Ibn 'Abbas said that Juwayriyya's name had been Barra and the Prophet,\nmay Allah bless him and grant him peace, had renamed her Juwayriyya."
"832","Abu Hurayra said, \Maymuna's name was Barra and then the Prophet"
"833","Here is the translated text in English:

He told us, Omar bin Hafs, he said: My father told us, he said: Al-A'mash told us, he said: Abu Sufyan told us, from Jabir, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, he said: If I were to live, I would guide my nation, if Allah willed it, one of them would be blessed with prosperity, and success, and not know harm. He said: Is it not Rafi'? They would say: Here is the blessing? So they would say: It is not here, and the Prophet, peace be upon him, would then withdraw from that."
"834","Jabir ibn 'Abdullah said, \The Prophet"
"835","He narrated to us Muhammad bin al-Mustannaa, who said: He narrated to us Umar bin Yunus bin al-Qasim, who said: He narrated to us Ikrima, from Simak, the father of Zumaail, who said: He narrated to me Abdullah bin Abbas, who said: He narrated to me Umar bin al-Khatab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Prophet (peace be upon him) left his wives, I was a young boy in Rabah, the servant of Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him), and I called out: O Rabah, ask permission for me to enter upon Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him)."
"836","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \Name yourselves with my name"
"837","Here is the translated text in English:Adam narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas bin Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) was in the market, when a man said: ""O Abu al-Qasim!"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) turned to him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I only called out to this one."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Name yourself after me, but do not nickname yourself after my kunyah."""
"838","Yusuf ibn 'Abdullah ibn Sallam said, \The Prophet"
"839","\He had a son and they wanted to name him Muhammad.\""]\nThe Prophet said"
"840","Abu Musa said, \I had a son and I brought him to the Prophet"
"841","Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab reported that his grandfather went to the\nProphet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace. He asked, \What is your\nname?\"" \""Hazn (rough)"
"842","Jabir said, \One of our men had a son and named him al-Qasim. The\nAnsar said"
"843","Ibn al-Hanafiyya was heard to say, \There was an allowance made\nfor 'Ali. He asked"
"844","Abu Hurayra said, \The Messenger of Allah"
"845","Abu Umar narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Prophet ﷺ was in the marketplace when a man said: ""O Aba al-Qasim!"" The Prophet ﷺ turned around. The man said: ""I called this one."" He said: ""Name yourselves by my name, but do not use my kunyah."""
